-box; usable = total * (1 - damage-percent/100); margin = usable - order-quantity; fulfillment = usable >= order-quantity. These are mathematical definitions, not empirical assumptions. The percentage-to-fraction conversion (divide by 100) is also fixed. No shipment-specific constants are captured; each application reads its own named cells.", :steps "1. Compute total-2 = 15*24 = 360. 2. Compute usable-2 = 360*(1-5/100) = 342. 3. Compute margin-2 = 342-350 = -8 (shortage). 4. Compute fulfillment-2 = 342>=350 = false. 5. Connect results to observed ports and text port.", :operators "+ - * / >= str", :status "all inputs known; computation is fully determined", :outputs "total items, usable stock, margin (surplus/shortage), fulfillment boolean for shipment-2", :operator "none", :units "boxes (count), items-per-box (count), damage-percent (percent 0-100), order-quantity (items), total (items), usable (items), margin (items)", :unknowns "none; all inputs are known", :facts "boxes-2=15, items-per-box-2=24, damage-percent-2=5 (inspection-confirmed), order-quantity-2=350", :parameters "boxes (count), items-per-box (count), damage-percent (percent 0-100), order-quantity (items). These four quantities vary between shipments; the arithmetic relationships connecting them to the four outputs are fixed.", :decision :reuse}, :selected-reference nil, :selected-callable false, :request-count 5, :identity {:id #uuid "fd8bf8d8-ba9b-4fc0-9a20-1e4bf18cd8aa", :run-id #uuid "260df912-6dea-425b-994e-7e0ccec82edd"}, :child #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "fa820676-d58c-32d5-b9fa-9301378067c8"}}]